        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int XSecure_RsaPrivateDecrypt</definition>
        <argsstring>(XSecure_ClientInstance *InstancePtr, const u64 KeyAddr, const u64 InDataAddr, const u32 Size, const u64 OutDataAddr)</argsstring>
        <name>XSecure_RsaPrivateDecrypt</name>
        <param>
          <type>XSecure_ClientInstance *</type>
          <declname>InstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const u64</type>
          <declname>KeyAddr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const u64</type>
          <declname>InDataAddr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const u32</type>
          <declname>Size</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const u64</type>
          <declname>OutDataAddr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sends IPI request to Perform RSA decryption with private key. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the client instance </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>KeyAddr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Address of the Key </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InDataAddr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Address of the data which has to be decrypted </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Key size in bytes, Input size also should be same as key size mentioned. Inputs supported are XSECURE_RSA_4096_KEY_SIZE, XSECURE_RSA_2048_KEY_SIZE, or XSECURE_RSA_3072_KEY_SIZE </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>OutDataAddr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Address of the buffer where resultant decrypted data to be stored</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS If the update is successful</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM On invalid input parameter</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE If there is a failure </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Return XST_INVALID_PARAM if InstancePtr or its MailboxPtr is NULL</para></listitem><listitem><para>Return XST_INVALID_PARAM if Size is a unsupported RSA key size</para></listitem><listitem><para>Link shared memory of size RsaParams to RsaParams structure for IPI usage. Validates the size of the shared memory whether the required size is available or not.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Fill Payload</para></listitem><listitem><para>Send request to PLM through generic request API. This internally handles SMC or IPI mailbox based on build configuration.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>        </inbodydescription>
